To compile a directory (resolve the globals):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Write in strong green "                      [OK]" then the CRLF string to Stdout.
  Write in strong blue " [05/16]" to StdOut.
  Write "  Resolving global symbols…" to Stdout.
  Start the resolving globals timer.
  Resolve the globals.
  Stop the resolving globals timer.

To resolve some globals:
  [Loop.]
    If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
    Get a global from the globals.
    If the global is nil, exit.
    Resolve the global.
  Repeat.

To resolve a global:
  If the global is nil, exit.
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  If the global's global body is not blank,
    Resolve the global (compile body).
  If the global's type name is blank,
    Abort with "Error #39. Expected a type name for global variable '" then the global's name then "'." and the global's locus;
    Exit.
  Resolve the global as a variable.

To resolve a global (compile body):
  If the global is nil, exit.
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Slap a rider on the global's global body.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  If the rider's token substring is not any literal,
    Abort with "Error #40. expected a literal for the global variable initializer. Found '" then the rider's token substring then "'." and the rider;
    Exit.
  Compile a literal given the rider.
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  If the rider's token substring is not blank,
    Abort with "Error #41. Is a period missing around here?" and the rider;
    Exit.
  If the global's type name is blank,
    Put the literal's type's name into the global's type name.
  Put the literal into the global's literal.
  Index the literal.

To compile a literal given a rider:
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Add the literal to the literals given the rider's token substring's first byte pointer.
  If the rider's token substring is any flag literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (flag);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any hex literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (hex);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any numeric literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (numeric);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any pointer literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (pointer);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any string literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (string);
    Exit.
  Abort with "Error #42. Internal error - compile a term given a rider (literal). The literal's data type could not be properly identified." and the rider.

To compile a literal given a rider (flag):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Convert the rider's token substring to a flag.
  Convert the flag to the literal's data.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Put "flag" into the literal's type name.
  Resolve the literal.

To resolve a variable:
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  If the variable is nil, exit.
  If the variable's type is not nil, exit.
  If the variable's type name is not blank,
    Resolve the variable (explicit type name);
    Exit.
  Find the variable's type and the variable's nickname given the variable's name.
  If the variable's type is not nil,
    Put the variable's type's name into the variable's type name;
    Exit.
  Abort with "Error #43. I can't find the '" then the variable's name then "' type." and the variable's locus.

To resolve a variable (explicit type name):
  Find the variable's type given the variable's type name and the type index.
  If the variable's type is nil,
    Abort with "Error #44. I can't find the '" then the variable's type name then "' type." and the variable's locus;
    Exit.

To find a type and a nickname given a name:
  Void the type.
  Clear the nickname.
  Slap a substring on the name.
  Loop.
    If the substring is blank, exit.
    Find the type given the substring and the type index.
    If the type is not nil, break.
    Skip to the next word in the substring.
  Repeat.
  Put the name's first byte pointer into another substring's first byte pointer.
  Put the substring's first byte pointer minus 2 into the other substring's last byte pointer.
  If the other substring is not blank,
    Put the other substring into the nickname.
  If the other substring is blank,
    Put the substring into the nickname.

To skip to the next word in a substring:
  [Loop.]
    If the substring is blank, exit.
      If the substring's first byte pointer's target is noise, break.
      Add 1 to the substring's first byte pointer.
  Repeat.
  Skip any leading noise in the substring.

To compile a literal given a rider (hex):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Put the rider's token substring into a nibble substring.
  Add 1 to the nibble substring's first byte pointer.
  Convert the nibble substring to the literal's data.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Put "hex string" into the literal's type name.
  Resolve the literal.

To convert a nibble substring to a string:
  Employ convert a nibble string to a hex string.

To compile a literal given a rider (numeric):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  If the rider is followed by any unit of measure,
    Compile the literal given the rider (numeric - with unit of measure);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any integer literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (numeric - integer);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any ratio literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (numeric - ratio);
    Exit.
  If the rider's token substring is any mixed literal,
    Compile the literal given the rider (numeric - ratio);
    Exit.

To decide if a rider is followed by any unit of measure:
  Privatize the rider.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  If the rider's token substring is not any name starter, say no.
  Scan a name given the rider.
  Find a type given the name and the type index.
  If the type is nil, say no.
  If the name is not "times", say yes. \ special because times is an infix operator and a unit of measure
  If the rider's token substring is the start of any expression, say no.
  Say yes.

To decide if a string is the start of any expression:
  If the string is any sign, say yes.
  If the string is any indefinite article, say yes.
  If the string is "the", say yes.
  If the string is any literal, say yes.
  Say no.

To compile a literal given a rider (numeric - with unit of measure):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Convert the rider's token substring to a ratio.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Scan a name given the rider.
  Find a type given the name and the type index.
  If the type is nil,
    Abort with "Error #45. '" then the name then "' is an invalid unit of measure." and the literal's locus;
    Exit.
  If the type cannot be reduced to "number",
    Abort with "Error #46.'" then the name then "' is an invalid unit of measure." and the literal's locus;
    Exit.
  Put the type's scale into a final ratio.
  If the type's scale is 0,
    Put 1/1 into the final ratio.
  Multiply the final ratio by the ratio.
  Reduce the final ratio.
  If the final ratio's denominator is 0,
    Abort with "Error #47. We seem to have an invalid unit of measure here." and the literal's locus.
  Put the final ratio's numerator divided by the final ratio's denominator into a number.
  Put the type's name into the literal's type name.
  Convert the number to the literal's data.
  Resolve the literal.

To compile a literal given a rider (numeric - integer):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Convert the rider's token substring to a number.
  Convert the number to the literal's data.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Put "number" into the literal's type name.
  Resolve the literal.

To compile a literal given a rider (numeric - ratio):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Convert the rider's token substring to a ratio.
  Convert the ratio to the literal's data.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Put "ratio" into the literal's type name.
  Resolve the literal.

To compile a literal given a rider (pointer):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Convert nil to the literal's data.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Put "pointer" into the literal's type name.
  Resolve the literal.

To compile a literal given a rider (string):
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  Put the rider's token substring into the literal's data.
  Unquote the literal's data.
  Move the rider (compiler rules).
  Put "string" into the literal's type name.
  Resolve the literal.

To index a literal:
  If the compiler's abort flag is set, exit.
  If the literal is nil, exit.
  If the literal's name is in the literal index,
    Abort with "Error #48. Internal error - index a literal" and the literal's locus;
    Exit.
  Index the literal given the literal's name and the literal index.



















